{
  "_comment": [
    "Single source of truth for which configuration keys the bot may receive.",
    "",
    "Generated from apex/settings_policy.py and read by BOTH sides:",
    "  server.js filters GET /api/bot-config down to these keys",
    "  apex/settings_policy asserts its own tables still match this file",
    "",
    "The alternative was a second copy of the allowlist written in JS, which is",
    "the version that drifts: the day someone adds a setting in Python and not",
    "in JS, the bot stops receiving it and nothing fails loudly.",
    "",
    "Regenerate with: python3 scripts/gen_bot_config_fields.py"
  ],
